                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I realize it's just one person doing all this coding, but...\nI guess I'm not \"hardcore\" enough.\nIt was good for a few minutes, but I couldn't get past all the negatives for very long.\nFirst, bad spelling and translations.\nSecond, awkward controls. I mean, Really!, why not have the JUMP be the one that grabs the ledge instead of a special YouAreHereToJump button.  And that's just for starters.\nThird, awful timing on deeds being done. Click podium, slowly pan to door, wait for door, admire that the door is now open, slowly pan back to podium, reflect for a moment on the amazing technology that opens doors, release controls to allow movement again.\nFourth, die a lot, and wait a while between attempts along with mouse-breaking clicking to get past the dialog. Again.",
